# WHAT THIS REPOSITORY IS FOR.
#
# Everything in this project that was WRITTEN. The shaders, the art tables, the
# plugin's C++, the session tooling, the config, and the licence record for
# every third-party asset. About six megabytes, and the only part that cannot
# be rebuilt from something else.
#
# What is left out is left out on purpose, and each line says why.

# Built by the engine, from the source that IS tracked. Four and a half
# gigabytes of it, rewritten on every build, and meaningless on another machine.
Binaries/
Intermediate/
DerivedDataCache/
Saved/
Build/Receipts/

# THE CONTENT AND THE ART ARE NOT HERE, AND ONE OF THE REASONS IS BINDING.
#
# The soft reason: Content/ is 857 MB of .uasset and Art/ is 1.7 GB of source
# meshes. Git without LFS handles neither well, and a repository that takes ten
# minutes to clone is a repository nobody clones.
#
# THE HARD REASON, which is not a decision to revisit: Art/Bestiary is under
# the Quaternius Asset License and NOT CC0. It allows shipping a built client
# containing the models and forbids redistributing the asset files themselves,
# so a repository carrying them would be redistributing them. Content/ holds
# the same models in imported form and is no different. Anybody tempted to put
# either directory back must read Art/Bestiary/README.md first and take that
# pack out, or the repository breaks a licence the moment it is pushed.
#
# The READMEs ARE tracked, and they are the whole point of the exception: the
# licence record is the one thing in that directory that cannot be downloaded
# again, and the pack whose licence matters most is the one whose record would
# otherwise never reach the repository.
Content/
Audio/
Art/**
!Art/**/
!Art/**/README.md

# Editor backups, written beside a file before a risky change and worth
# nothing once the change is green. Same rule as the bridge's.
*.before-*
*.bak

# Scratch written by the session tooling: a camera transform, a PIE option
# block, a stop request. Regenerated on every call.
Tools/_*.json

logs/
*.log
.DS_Store

# Generated by Xcode from the uproject, and it carries a per-user path.
*.xcworkspace/

# This machine's own session settings, not the project's.
.claude/
.mcp.json

# Packaged clients. `interval-ios.ipa` is 383 MB of built app: the whole point
# of tracking the source is that this can be made again from it.
*.ipa
*.app/
*.dmg

# Python bytecode, written beside the tooling on every run.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
